reers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4687-Research-Fellow-109857-0826/en-GB</id>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4687-Research-Fellow-109857-0826/en-GB?instant=apply\" type=\"text/html\"/>\n    <title>Research Fellow (109857-0826)</title>\n    <updated>2026-08-19T15:57:11Z</updated>\n    <published>2026-08-19T15:57:11Z</published>\n    <content type=\"xhtml\">\n      <div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Title:Research Fellow (109857-0826)<br/>\nPosition Type:Fixed Term<br/>\n</div>\n    </content>\n  </entry>\n  <entry xml:base=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4680-Research-Fellow-x2-112040-0826/en-GB\">\n    <id>https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4680-Research-Fellow-x2-112040-0826/en-GB</id>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4680-Research-Fellow-x2-112040-0826/en-GB?instant=apply\" type=\"text/html\"/>\n    <title>Research Fellow x2 (112040-0826)</title>\n    <updated>2026-08-17T13:54:14Z</updated>\n    <published>2026-08-17T13:54:14Z</published>\n    <content type=\"xhtml\">\n      <div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Title:Research Fellow x2 (112040-0826)<br/>\nPosition Type:Fixed Term<br/>\n</div>\n    </content>\n  </entry>\n  <entry xml:base=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4669-Research-Fellow-112033-0826/en-GB\">\n    <id>https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4669-Research-Fellow-112033-0826/en-GB</id>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4669-Research-Fellow-112033-0826/en-GB?instant=apply\" type=\"text/html\"/>\n    <title>Research Fellow (112033-0826)</title>\n    <updated>2026-08-14T10:30:35Z</updated>\n    <published>2026-08-14T10:30:35Z</published>\n    <content type=\"xhtml\">\n      <div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Title:Research Fellow (112033-0826)<br/>\nPosition Type:Fixed Term<br/>\n</div>\n    </content>\n  </entry>\n  <entry xml:base=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4638-Tutor-111433-0826/en-GB\">\n    <id>https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4638-Tutor-111433-0826/en-GB</id>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4638-Tutor-111433-0826/en-GB?instant=apply\" type=\"text/html\"/>\n    <title>Tutor (111433-0826)</title>\n    <updated>2026-08-11T09:59:01Z</updated>\n    <published>2026-08-11T09:59:01Z</published>\n    <content type=\"xhtml\">\n      <div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Title:Tutor (111433-0826)<br/>\nPosition Type:Fixed Term<br/>\n</div>\n    </content>\n  </entry>\n  <entry xml:base=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4615-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Director-of-Student-Projects-111941-0826/en-GB\">\n    <id>https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4615-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Director-of-Student-Projects-111941-0826/en-GB</id>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4615-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Director-of-Student-Projects-111941-0826/en-GB?instant=apply\" type=\"text/html\"/>\n    <title>Assistant or Associate Professor (Director of Student Projects) (111941-0826)</title>\n    <updated>2026-08-05T14:21:07Z</updated>\n    <published>2026-08-05T14:21:07Z</published>\n    <content type=\"xhtml\">\n      <div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Title:Assistant or Associate Professor (Director of Student Projects) (111941-0826)<br/>\nPosition Type:Permanent<br/>\n</div>\n    </content>\n  </entry>\n  <entry xml:base=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4533-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Climate-Resilient-Infrastructure-and-Transport-Systems-111893-0726/en-GB\">\n    <id>https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4533-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Climate-Resilient-Infrastructure-and-Transport-Systems-111893-0726/en-GB</id>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4533-Assistant-or-Associate-Professor-Climate-Resilient-Infrastructure-and-Transport-Systems-111893-0726/en-GB?instant=apply\" type=\"text/html\"/>\n    <title>Assistant or Associate Professor (Climate-Resilient Infrastructure and Transport Systems) (111893-0726)</title>\n    <updated>2026-07-24T12:30:01Z</updated>\n    <published>2026-07-24T12:30:01Z</published>\n    <content type=\"xhtml\">\n      <div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Title:Assistant or Associate Professor (Climate-Resilient Infrastructure and Transport Systems) (111893-0726)<br/>\nPosition Type:Permanent<br/>\n</div>\n    </content>\n  </entry>\n  <entry xml:base=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4311-Assistant-Professor-Research-Teaching-105617-0626/en-GB\">\n    <id>https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4311-Assistant-Professor-Research-Teaching-105617-0626/en-GB</id>\n    <link rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/mobile-0/appcentre-ext/brand-4/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4311-Assistant-Professor-Research-Teaching-105617-0626/en-GB?instant=apply\" type=\"text/html\"/>\n    <title>Assistant Professor (Research &amp; Teaching) (105617-0626)</title>\n    <updated>2026-06-08T14:43:24Z</updated>\n    <published>2026-06-08T14:43:24Z</published>\n    <content type=\"xhtml\">\n      <div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Title:Assistant Professor (Research &amp; Teaching) (105617-0626)<br/>\nPosition Type:Permanent<br/>\n</div>\n    </content>\n  </entry>\n</feed>"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4716-Research-Assistant-108927-0826/en-GB": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (108927-0826)",
      "description": "Research Assistant (108927-0826) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Research Assistant (108927-0826) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Economics Position Type Fixed Term Duration Fixed-term contract for 12 months Salary £31,236 to £34,610 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Federico Rossi, Associate Professor, at Federico.Rossi@warwick.ac.uk. The Research Assistant will support the Project Lead Federico Rossi and collaborators in the successful execution of the project “ Human Capital, the Organization of Production and Economic Development” funded by an ERC/UKRI Starting Grant 2023. The project will leverage micro-level data from multiple countries and novel theoretical frameworks to shed light on how the accumulation and utilization of different types of skills is shaped by and can facilitate the adaptation to some of the most pressing challenges faced by the global economy: population ageing, climate change, and the reallocation of workers across economic activities. The position is particularly suitable for someone interested in pursuing a PhD in Economics or related fields. Pre-doctoral Research Assistants previously working on this project have been admitted to prestigious PhD programs at New York University and Imperial College London. The Research Assistant will benefit from extensive mentoring from the Project Leader and his collaborators and will have the opportunity to develop several skills useful for conducting academic research. About You We require an individual who has an interest in the research area, who is pro-active and willing to work as part of a team. The work will involve collecting and harmonizing micro-level data from countries at different levels of development to construct novel facts on the accumulation and utilization of human skills in a variety of contexts. The Research Assistant will also collaborate to the development and estimation of theoretical models that will be used to assess the impacts of several educational and training policies on economic development. The job will involve close collaboration and frequent interactions with the Project Leader and his collaborators. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department The Department of Economics has become widely regarded as one of the top economics department in the UK and Europe. We consistently rank highly in leading UK and international subject league tables and are currently ranked 1st in the Good University Guide 2026. In the Research Excellence Framework (REF) 2021, which assesses the quality of research in UK higher education institutions, 99% of the Department’s research was rated world-leading or internationally excellent - placing us 2nd in the UK for economics. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Wednesday 02 September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: TBC Start Date: 01 October 2026 (flexible) * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 26 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD - Research Assistant (108927).pdf – 132KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. This opportunity is closed to applications. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4576-Employee-Mobility-Officer-111956-0726/en-GB": {
      "title": "Employee Mobility Officer (111956-0726)",
      "description": "Employee Mobility Officer (111956-0726) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Employee Mobility Officer (111956-0726) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department People Team Position Type Permanent Salary £35,608 to £46,049 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Tom Such (Head of People Insight and Operational Excellence) at Thomas.Such@warwick.ac.uk. Flexible Working We will consider applications for employment on a part-time basis. In particular, we welcome applications from candidates seeking a minimum of 21.9 hours per week (0.6 FTE). This is an opportunity to take a leading role in the University’s international working and employee mobility service, helping colleagues and departments navigate the practical, financial and compliance considerations associated with working overseas. As Employee Mobility Officer, you will lead the day-to-day delivery of the service and manage the Employee Mobility team, setting priorities, overseeing casework and supporting colleagues to provide a consistent and responsive service. You will manage complex and sensitive international working cases, ensuring that the appropriate information, approvals and documentation are in place and that higher-risk matters are identified and escalated appropriately. You will work closely with colleagues across Payroll, Expenses, Finance, Tax, Legal and the wider People Team, as well as with external specialist advisers, to coordinate effective and compliant cross-border arrangements. The role also offers the opportunity to lead mobility-related projects, improve systems and workflows, and contribute operational insight to the continued development of the University’s approach to international working. About You You will bring experience of leading or supervising colleagues within an operational, casework or compliance-focused environment. You will be comfortable setting priorities, providing guidance and maintaining high standards while managing competing demands and deadlines. You will have experience coordinating structured approval, governance or case-management processes and handling complex or sensitive cases that require sound judgement. You will be able to interpret and apply policies consistently, identify risks and recognise when specialist advice or escalation is required. Strong communication and relationship-building skills will be important, as you will work with a wide range of colleagues and translate complex considerations into clear, practical guidance. You will also understand the importance of accurate, auditable records, data integrity and effective use of HR or case-management systems. You will be interested in improving how services operate and willing to contribute ideas that strengthen processes, systems and the experience of those using the service. Previous experience of international working, employee mobility or cross-border arrangements would be valuable, although the ability to learn, collaborate and exercise sound professional judgement will be equally important. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department This role sits within the University’s revised Employee Mobility and Immigration Services function, part of the People Insight and Operational Excellence team within the People Team. It is an important time to join the department as we continue to evolve our services in response to a changing institutional, employment and regulatory environment. The team is at the forefront of this work, helping to shape how the People Team responds to digital innovation, technological change, artificial intelligence and new approaches to delivering efficient, effective and user-focused services. People Insight and Operational Excellence supports the continued development of the People Team and helps the wider University achieve its strategic objectives. This includes improving systems and processes, strengthening the use of data and technology, and developing services that are responsive to the changing needs of colleagues and the institution. International staff mobility and the ability to engage talent from across the world are central to the University’s ambitions. The Employee Mobility and Immigration Services function enables this by helping departments manage overseas working arrangements effectively, coordinating specialist advice and ensuring that decisions are supported by clear governance and accurate information. This role offers the opportunity to join a developing service and make a direct contribution to the University’s global ambitions. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Wednesday 2nd September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include a CV and Cover Letter. These documents should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: 22nd September 2026 Start Date: 1st October 2026 * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 30 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD Employee Mobility Officer (111956).pdf – 128KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. This opportunity is closed to applications. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4575-Immigration-Services-Officer-111957-0726/en-GB": {
      "title": "Immigration Services Officer (111957-0726)",
      "description": "Immigration Services Officer (111957-0726) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Immigration Services Officer (111957-0726) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department People Team Position Type Permanent Salary £35,608 to £46,049 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Tom Such (Head of People Insight and Operational Excellence) at Thomas.Such@warwick.ac.uk. Flexible Working We will consider applications for employment on a part-time basis. In particular, we welcome applications from candidates seeking a minimum of 21.9 hours per week (0.6 FTE). This is an opportunity to take a leading operational role within the University’s Employee Mobility and Immigration Services Team, helping to deliver a high-quality, compliant and supportive immigration service for colleagues from across the world. As Immigration Services Officer, you will provide specialist advice across sponsored visa routes, other UK work visas, visitor routes and right to work requirements. You will manage complex and sensitive cases, oversee sponsorship compliance and act as the first point of escalation for Immigration Coordinators and University departments. You will also supervise and develop members of the team, providing technical guidance, quality assurance and support with workload management. The role combines detailed casework with broader responsibility for service quality and continuous improvement. You will help ensure that the University’s records and processes remain accurate, consistent and ready for audit, while identifying opportunities to improve guidance, systems and ways of working. You will work closely with colleagues across the People Team and the wider University, translating complex immigration requirements into clear and practical advice. About You You will bring strong working knowledge of UK immigration sponsorship and right to work requirements, including experience of Skilled Worker and related visa routes. You will be confident interpreting immigration rules and applying them consistently, while recognising when cases require careful judgement or escalation. You will have experience managing complex, sensitive or high-risk cases within a regulated environment and will be comfortable balancing service needs with legal and compliance responsibilities. Strong attention to detail will be essential, alongside the ability to maintain accurate, auditable records and manage competing deadlines. You will also be an effective and supportive team leader, able to supervise colleagues, provide technical guidance and promote consistent standards across the service. Your communication skills will enable you to explain complex requirements clearly and provide practical, accurate advice to colleagues and stakeholders at all levels. We are looking for someone who combines technical expertise with sound judgement, a collaborative approach and a commitment to delivering an approachable and responsive service. You will be motivated to improve processes, strengthen compliance and use systems and technology effectively to enhance the experience of both colleagues and service users. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department This role sits within the University’s newly revised Employee Mobility and Immigration Services function, part of the People Insight and Operational Excellence team within the wider People Team. It is an exciting time to join the department as we continue to evolve our services in response to a changing institutional, employment and regulatory environment. The team is at the forefront of this work, helping to shape how the People Team responds to digital innovation, technological change, artificial intelligence and new ways of delivering efficient, effective and user-focused services. People Insight and Operational Excellence plays an important role in supporting the continued development of the People Team and enabling the wider University to achieve its strategic objectives. This includes improving systems and processes, strengthening the use of data and technology, and developing services that are responsive to the changing needs of colleagues and the institution. Attracting, engaging and supporting talented staff from across the world is central to the University’s ambitions. The Employee Mobility and Immigration Services function enables this by providing expert, compliant and practical support to international colleagues, managers and departments. This role offers an opportunity to join a developing service and make a direct contribution to the University’s ability to recruit and retain global talent. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Wednesday 2nd September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include a CV and Cover Letter. These documents should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: 24 September 2026 Start Date: 1st October 2026 * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 30 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD Immigration Services Officer (111957).pdf – 148KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. This opportunity is closed to applications. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4582-Assistant-Campus-Cleaning-Services-Manager-77928-0726/en-GB": {
      "title": "Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager (77928-0726)",
      "description": "Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager (77928-0726) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager (77928-0726) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Estates - Campus & Cleaning Services Position Type Permanent Hours 35 hours per week Salary £26,707 to £30,378 per annum pro rata About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Donna Graham (Donna Graham) at D.T.Stanton@warwick.ac.uk. Campus Cleaning Services provides cleaning across 7,076 campus bedrooms, 479 hotel rooms and 65 University buildings. We are looking for an Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager to join the Non-Residential Campus Cleaning Services team within the Estates Department. We are looking for an individual to assist in leading the team to achieve quality standards, maintain systems and safety procedures and to deliver a cost effective, efficient and customer focused Assistant Management. To support and deputise for the Campus Cleaning Services Manager. You will manage a team of cleaning staff. This role offers a great opportunity to manage and improve Campus Cleaning Services in a lively environment. You will oversee daily operations, manage staff and ensure high cleaning standards. This position gives you the chance to work with various teams and contribute to a more efficient and sustainable campus. Please note the shift pattern will vary between the below 12.30pm-8.30pm, 2pm-10pm,11.30am – 7.30pm with a 1 hour lunch break, 5 over 7 days and some weekend work may be required. About You We are looking for a person with extensive management experience who: Has led large teams (80+ staff) and knows how to motivate and organise them effectively Can plan and allocate resources efficiently throughout the year Has experience managing budgets and procurement Understands quality control and can address performance issues Knows health and safety regulations related to cleaning Can handle multiple tasks and deadlines Provides excellent customer service to students and visitors Communicates well with team members Can work flexibly, including some late evenings and weekends when needed If you are a practical person, results driven leader looking for a hands-on management role, we would love to hear from you. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department For further information about Campus & Cleaning Services , please visit our website. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Thursday 3rd September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: To be confirmed Start Date: To be confirmed * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 26 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD Assistant Campus Cleaning Services Manager (77928).pdf – 126KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4634-UX-Executive-109512-0826/en-GB": {
      "title": "UX Executive ‎(109512-0826)",
      "description": "UX Executive ‎(109512-0826) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account UX Executive ‎(109512-0826) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Chief Communications Officers' Group - Marketing & Student Recruitment Position Type Permanent Salary £31,236 to £34,610 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Matthew Fife (UX Designer) at Matthew.Fife@warwick.ac.uk Are you passionate about user-centred design and creating digital experiences that make a real difference? Join the University of Warwick's Creative & Digital team and help shape the experience of one of the UK's leading university websites and digital platforms. Supporting audiences that include prospective students, current students, staff, researchers and members of the public, you'll contribute to digital services used by thousands of people every day. Working alongside experienced UX, digital and content specialists, you'll have the opportunity to develop your skills across the full user experience lifecycle, from research and testing through to user journeys, information architecture, wireframing and prototyping. You'll lead smaller UX projects independently while contributing to larger strategic initiatives that influence the University's digital future. This role offers a unique combination of professional development, meaningful impact and variety. You'll work with stakeholders from across the University, helping to champion accessibility, evidence-based design and user-centred thinking while delivering digital experiences that support Warwick's global reputation for excellence in education and research. As part of a collaborative and supportive team, you'll be encouraged to bring new ideas, develop your expertise and play an important role in advancing the University's digital ambitions. About You We're looking for someone who is passionate about creating accessible, user-centred digital experiences and is keen to develop their UX expertise within a collaborative digital team. You'll bring experience of user experience design methods, user research and requirements gathering, with an understanding of how user insight can be translated into effective digital solutions. You have knowledge of contemporary UX principles and accessibility best practice, and you're comfortable using tools such as Figma to create wireframes, prototypes and user journeys. You are an effective communicator who can build positive relationships with stakeholders, facilitate discussions and confidently explain design decisions based on user needs and evidence. You enjoy working collaboratively with designers, content specialists, developers and project stakeholders to deliver successful outcomes. You'll be organised, able to manage your own workload and projects, and comfortable working across multiple priorities. Experience of HTML and CSS would be beneficial, particularly when working with development teams to implement and refine digital experiences. Most importantly, you'll be enthusiastic about advocating for users, continuously improving digital experiences and helping to embed user-centred design practices across the University. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department This role sits in the Marketing, Communications, Insight and Student Recruitment department (MCI&SR), at the heart of the University. Working with us means that no two days will be the same as we offer a place of possibility and challenge where you will find a supportive environment with the scope to learn, grow, make an impact, and develop your career. In MCI & Student Recruitment, we’re proud to work within a framework of values that we’ve co-created and agreed. These describe the way in which we as a team behave towards each other and the way we work. For that reason, our recruitment process will include two interviews – one based on capabilities and the other behaviours based. More information will be shared with candidates who progress to interview stage. Our co-created values will be key for applicants to demonstrate. They are: CREATIVITY: Thinking innovatively of bold solutions COLLABORATION: Working together to make things happen AMBITION: Committing to achieving great results and impact RESPECT: Valuing and including diverse voices and perspectives If you are passionate about user experience, possess the skills to engage effectively with a wide range of stakeholders, and are excited by the opportunity to help shape and improve Warwick's digital experiences, then we want to hear from you. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 6th September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: To be confirmed Start Date: To be confirmed * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 26 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD - UX Executive ‎(109512).pdf – 169KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4735-Teaching-Fellow-103423-0826/en-GB": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow (103423-0826)",
      "description": "Teaching Fellow (103423-0826) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Teaching Fellow (103423-0826) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Warwick Business School Position Type Fixed Term Duration Fixed-term contract for 3 years Salary £35,608 to £46,049 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries, please contact Andrea Isoni, Professor of Behavioural Science, at Andrea.Isoni@wbs.ac.uk . Flexible Working We will consider applications for employment on a part-time basis, down to a minimum of 0.8 FTE. The Behavioural Science Group are recruiting for a Teaching Fellow post for the next academic year (2026/27). The position is fixed term for a period of 36 months. The Behavioural Science Group is a highly multidisciplinary team, drawn from psychology, economics, data science, and beyond. We are bound together by a vision of understanding, predicting, and guiding human behaviour in the widest possible range of contexts. Our interests, approaches and styles overlap with those of other members of the group in different ways. This allows us to be highly innovative. We routinely use laboratory, field and online experiments, mathematical and economic modelling, and large datasets to explore and to test and develop theory. Teaching at WBS is very rewarding. We offer comprehensive admin support and a thriving teaching environment. Each group is supported by a dedicated teaching and learning consultant, who provides assistance with the design and preparation of teaching materials and in the adoption of the latest learning technologies, including a state-of-the-art smart stage. You will benefit from development opportunities through regular workshops, yearly teaching and learning symposia and dedicated workload allocation for scholarship of teaching and learning. About You You will be required to undertake high quality teaching at postgraduate and undergraduate level to support the work of the Group and the School and develop and enhance their teaching reputation, both internally and externally. You will help to ensure high quality learning and teaching aligned with current and emerging industry practices. You will assist in the organisation and delivery of a range of extracurricular activities to help with the promotion of the school and its taught programmes. You will be able to teach statistics and big data analytics at undergraduate and postgraduate level and be familiar with statistical packages such as R. You will be expected to deliver lectures, seminars and workshops to groups of different sizes and students enrolled in programmes ranging from undergraduate degrees to pre- and post-experience masters. You will set and mark assignments, coordinate the work of graduate teaching assistants, and interface with our experienced admin and support teams in the management of online teaching materials and other resources. You will undertake other teaching-related duties in agreement with the Dean and the Head of Group. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department Warwick Business School (WBS) is a place where big ideas meet real impact. We’re part of a world-class university, but we’re more than just our reputation. For nearly 60 years, we’ve been helping people turn ambition into action, equipping them to make a real difference in the world. Please view our online brochure , specifically created for candidates, to gain further insight into working at Warwick Business School. About Us We were the first UK business school to achieve triple accreditation (EQUIS, AMBA, AACSB), and our programmes consistently rank among the best - view all of our rankings here . But what really sets us apart is how it feels to be here. We’re down to earth, collaborative, and proud to create a place where staff, students and alumni feel at home. We want your time here to be as inspiring as it is rewarding, with the support, trust, and opportunities you need to grow both professionally and personally. Our Vision The world needs smart ideas, and the leaders who can bring them to life. Those ideas only matter if they can be put into practice. Our vision is simple: to shape the people and ideas that will define what comes next and ensure they have everything they need to make it happen. Everything we do is underpinned by our CORE values and fuelled by a Change Maker mindset. We look for this shared commitment in everyone who joins our community. We nurture that mindset every day by creating a workplace where curiosity is encouraged, ideas are shared openly, and everyone has the chance to turn bold thinking into meaningful action. Change Makers See the bigger picture. They think beyond themselves, seek out different perspectives, and consider the ripple effect of their actions. Challenge the norm. They question the status quo and look for better ways to make a difference. Have the drive to deliver. They don’t just imagine change; they put in the work to make it happen. Our CORE Values Curiosity. We challenge, explore, and create to build a better future. Openness. We welcome ideas, feedback, and change to keep moving forward. Restlessness. We’re never content to stand still; we keep striving for more. Excellence. We hold ourselves to the highest standards in everything we do. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 06 September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: TBC Start Date: TBC * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 30 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion Equality, Diversity, & Inclusion Warwick is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive and respectful community where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all backgrounds, cultures, and communities, and actively encourage candidates from underrepresented groups to apply. Find out more about our Social Inclusion work at Warwick . Find out more about our awards and accreditations . We are also one of the six founder institutions of the EUTOPIA European University Alliance . Safeguarding & DBS The University of Warwick is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of all those we work with. Roles involving regulated activity are subject to a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check at the appropriate level, in line with the DBS Code of Practice. The University will ensure that anyone subject to a barring order does not undertake any work with the barred group (children and/or adults). All employees, volunteers, and partners are expected to share our commitment to safeguarding. Rehabilitation of Ex-Offenders The University will not discriminate against applicants who make a disclosure relating to a conviction. Disclosures at application stage are only visible to the DBS team, not to hiring panels. This ensures fairness and removes bias from the shortlisting process. Job Description JD - Teaching Fellow (103423).pdf – 99KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK and/or are seeking sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa, please follow this link which contains further information about obtaining the right to work in the UK. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4727-Research-Fellow-in-Power-Electronics-112105-0826/en-GB": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Power Electronics (112105-0826)",
      "description": "Research Fellow in Power Electronics (112105-0826) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Research Fellow in Power Electronics (112105-0826) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department School of Engineering Position Type Fixed Term Duration Fixed-term contract for 12 months (ending no later than 31/12/2027) Salary £35,608 to £46,049 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries, please contact Professor Layi Alatise at O.Alatise@warwick.ac.uk. The School of Engineering is seeking a Research Fellow in Power Electronics to assist the Principal Investigator (Professor Layi Alatise) and the project collaborators in the successful execution of the research programme focused on power semiconductor devices and power electronics systems. The successful candidate will be responsible for designing, developing, and assembling power electronics test systems for the power semiconductor devices. You will undertake experimental research, analyse technical data, and use emerging developments within the power electronics field to inform and shape future research activities. A key aspect of the position will be disseminating research of findings through publication in leading international journals  and other reputable outlets. You will also contribute to the preparation of research proposals and applications to external funding bodies, helping to support and expand the project's research agenda. You will be expected to communicate complex information both orally and in writing  on material of a specialist or highly technical nature. This post is based at the University of Warwick. The successful candidate will be required to make occasional trips to collaborators/ specialist research facilities, so the willingness to travel occasionally is required. There will be opportunities for presenting work at international conferences. About You You will have a PhD or equivalent in Power Electronics/Electrical Engineering. You will have good knowledge and practical experience in power electronics and power semiconductor device characterisation, and a strong record of publications and research outputs in experimental Power Electronics. The ideal candidate will have strong communication skills including the ability to communicate effectively in English, both verbally and in writing. You will also have demonstrable ability to work collaboratively and effectively with academic and administrative colleagues, both within and outside the University, to promote a collegial environment, while contributing to the life and community of the school through various duties, such as supporting offer holder days and outreach activities, which may occasionally require weekend work. You will have good IT skills including Microsoft Office and proven ability to use IT to write technical research papers and presentations. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. PhD Status If you are near submission of your PhD, or have not yet had it conferred, any offers of employment will be made at Research Assistant level, at the highest spinal point of pay grade 5 (£34,610 per annum). Upon receipt of evidence confirming the successful award of your PhD, you will be promoted to Research Fellow , at the lowest spinal point of grade 6 (£35,608 per annum). About the Department The School of Engineering is one of the leading unified engineering schools in the UK and is currently ranked one of the top 10 engineering schools in all the major UK league tables. The University aims to promote work life balance for all employees and the School of Engineering will consider a range of possible flexible working arrangements in order to recruit the best candidate. The School of Engineering is committed to the principles of the Athena SWAN Charter, which recognises work undertaken to address gender equality, representation and progression for all staff working in an academic environment. The School currently holds the Athena SWAN Silver award and the University holds an Institutional Silver award. Further information about the work of the School in relation to Athena SWAN can be found at the following link: Athena SWAN - School of Engineering - University of Warwick About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 6th September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include a CV and Cover Letter. These documents should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: To be confirmed Start Date: To be confirmed * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 30 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion Equality, Diversity, & Inclusion Warwick is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive and respectful community where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all backgrounds, cultures, and communities, and actively encourage candidates from underrepresented groups to apply. Find out more about our Social Inclusion work at Warwick . Find out more about our awards and accreditations . We are also one of the six founder institutions of the EUTOPIA European University Alliance . Safeguarding & DBS The University of Warwick is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of all those we work with. Roles involving regulated activity are subject to a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check at the appropriate level, in line with the DBS Code of Practice. The University will ensure that anyone subject to a barring order does not undertake any work with the barred group (children and/or adults). All employees, volunteers, and partners are expected to share our commitment to safeguarding. Rehabilitation of Ex-Offenders The University will not discriminate against applicants who make a disclosure relating to a conviction. Disclosures at application stage are only visible to the DBS team, not to hiring panels. This ensures fairness and removes bias from the shortlisting process. Job Description JD - Research Fellow in Power Electronics (112105).pdf – 99KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK and/or are seeking sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa, please follow this link which contains further information about obtaining the right to work in the UK. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
