    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4655-Biomedical-Services-Unit-Technician-102657-0826/en-GB": {
      "title": "Biomedical Services Unit Technician (102657-0826)",
      "description": "Biomedical Services Unit Technician (102657-0826) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Biomedical Services Unit Technician (102657-0826) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Research Technology Platforms Position Type Permanent Salary £25,528 per annum About the Role Previous candidates need not apply. Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Sara Goulding (Deputy BSU Manager & NTCO) at Sara.goulding@warwick.ac.uk Applications are invited for the opportunity to join a friendly and dedicated team responsible for ensuring a high level of laboratory animal welfare (rodents and fish) and husbandry in accordance with the Animal Scientific Procedures Act (ASPA) 1986. You will be supervised in the management of wildtype breeding colonies and work as part of a team to ensure all animal accommodation and areas of the holding facility are cleaned regularly as well as carrying out daily health and environment checks according to ASPA. About You The successful candidate will have a passion for animal welfare and have knowledge of the requirements of the Animal (Scientific Procedure) Act 1986 which governs the use of animals in scientific research. They will also have excellent team working skills whilst also happy to work independently, educated to GCSE level or equivalent, undertake their day-to-day work with an eye for detail and cost effectiveness and have very good communication skills. The role will also be key in keeping accurate records in accordance with local guidelines and national legislation. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department The successful candidate will be working in one of the University’s Research Technology Platforms (RTP). Our RTPs provide an integrated network of world-class technologies needed to carry out outstanding research. Our facilities are available both for researchers at Warwick and for our external partners from industry and academia. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 6th September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: To be confirmed Start Date: To be confirmed * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 26 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD Biomedical Services Unit Technician (102657).pdf – 110KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4725-Global-Alumni-Engagement-Manager-106311-0826/en-GB": {
      "title": "Global Alumni Engagement Manager (106311-0826)",
      "description": "Global Alumni Engagement Manager (106311-0826) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Global Alumni Engagement Manager (106311-0826) This is a re-advertisement. Previous candidates for this role need not apply. Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Warwick Business School Position Type Fixed Term Duration Fixed-term contract for 12 months. Salary £47,389 - £56,535 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries, please contact  Sarah Jackson (Associate Director of Global Alumni Engagement) at sarah.jackson@wbs.ac.uk We are looking for a dynamic and talented Global Alumni Engagement Manager to help deliver a strategy that builds strong networks and lifelong relationships across sectors and geographies. You’ll play a key role in driving engagement through inspiring communications, building communities, events and a valued alumni benefits package. About You This alumni engagement role is central to building a vibrant global WBS community and would suit a pro-active and experienced alumni engagement professional. You will be a natural communicator with excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to engage confidently with alumni and stakeholders at all levels. You will be skilled at developing effective communication strategies for diverse global audiences, have experience of rolling out online platforms, managing online communities, creating compelling marketing collateral, and promoting a valued package of alumni benefits and services to maximise engagement across different community groups. With experience of delivering events for global audiences, you will be comfortable designing and managing a varied programme of activities—both online and in‑person—across multiple geographies and time zones. You will have substantial experience of working in a purpose-driven alumni or stakeholder engagement role, proven ability to recruit, manage and motivate volunteers, experience of line managing and developing staff, a global mindset, and the ability to build trust and influence others. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department In return you will have the opportunity to work for one of the world’s leading business schools. This is an exciting time to join a team of committed and capable colleagues in a stimulating environment where you will be contributing to valuable and impactful engagement strategies. The role will necessitate local, national and some international travel. Flexibility in hours will be required for some evening and weekend work. Warwick Business School (WBS) is a place where big ideas meet real impact. We’re part of a world-class university, but we’re more than just our reputation. For nearly 60 years, we’ve been helping people turn ambition into action, equipping them to make a real difference in the world. Please view our online brochure , specifically created for candidates, to gain further insight into working at Warwick Business School. About Us We were the first UK business school to achieve triple accreditation (EQUIS, AMBA, AACSB), and our programmes consistently rank among the best - view all of our rankings here . But what really sets us apart is how it feels to be here. We’re down to earth, collaborative, and proud to create a place where staff, students and alumni feel at home. We want your time here to be as inspiring as it is rewarding, with the support, trust, and opportunities you need to grow both professionally and personally. Our Vision The world needs smart ideas, and the leaders who can bring them to life. Those ideas only matter if they can be put into practice. Our vision is simple: to shape the people and ideas that will define what comes next and ensure they have everything they need to make it happen. Everything we do is underpinned by our CORE values and fuelled by a Change Maker mindset. We look for this shared commitment in everyone who joins our community. We nurture that mindset every day by creating a workplace where curiosity is encouraged, ideas are shared openly, and everyone has the chance to turn bold thinking into meaningful action. Change Makers See the bigger picture. They think beyond themselves, seek out different perspectives, and consider the ripple effect of their actions. Challenge the norm. They question the status quo and look for better ways to make a difference. Have the drive to deliver. They don’t just imagine change; they put in the work to make it happen. Our CORE Values Curiosity. We challenge, explore, and create to build a better future. Openness. We welcome ideas, feedback, and change to keep moving forward. Restlessness. We’re never content to stand still; we keep striving for more. Excellence. We hold ourselves to the highest standards in everything we do. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 6 September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: TBC Start Date: ASAP * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 30 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion Equality, Diversity, & Inclusion Warwick is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive and respectful community where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all backgrounds, cultures, and communities, and actively encourage candidates from underrepresented groups to apply. Find out more about our Social Inclusion work at Warwick . Find out more about our awards and accreditations . We are also one of the six founder institutions of the EUTOPIA European University Alliance . Safeguarding & DBS The University of Warwick is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of all those we work with. Roles involving regulated activity are subject to a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check at the appropriate level, in line with the DBS Code of Practice. The University will ensure that anyone subject to a barring order does not undertake any work with the barred group (children and/or adults). All employees, volunteers, and partners are expected to share our commitment to safeguarding. Rehabilitation of Ex-Offenders The University will not discriminate against applicants who make a disclosure relating to a conviction. Disclosures at application stage are only visible to the DBS team, not to hiring panels. This ensures fairness and removes bias from the shortlisting process. Job Description JD - Global Alumni Engagement Manager (106311).pdf – 92KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK and/or are seeking sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa, please follow this link which contains further information about obtaining the right to work in the UK. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4718-Curator-Art-Collection-20621-0826/en-GB": {
      "title": "Curator (Art Collection) (20621-0826)",
      "description": "Curator (Art Collection) (20621-0826) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Curator (Art Collection) (20621-0826) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Warwick Arts Centre Position Type Permanent Salary £35,608 - £46,049 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries, please contact Olivia Brook, Recruitment Manager, at Olivia.Brook.1@warwick.ac.uk . Join us as Art Collection Curator and play a central role in the day-to-day care, management and interpretation of a significant university art collection of over 1,000 works displayed across campus. Working closely with the Principal Curator, you will ensure that collections management activities including loans, documentation, conservation programmes and installations, are delivered to the highest professional standards and in line with Accreditation requirements. You will lead on the operational delivery of displays and installations across campus, collaborating with academic departments, students and stakeholders to realise projects that support teaching, research and the student experience. You will contribute to research, interpretation and engagement activity, developing content for digital platforms, exhibitions, talks and learning programmes that broaden access to the collection. The role works closely with the Principal Curator, Visual Arts Technician, Arts Centre colleagues, academic departments and the Art Collection Committee, as well as external artists, lenders, contractors and conservators. This is a varied, campus-wide role involving regular on-site activity across university locations and occasional off-site work. Flexibility is required to support installations, events and engagement activity, including some evening or weekend working. About You We are seeking a collaborative, organised and intellectually curious individual with a strong understanding of modern and contemporary art practice and an awareness of the gallery and museum sector. You will bring a thoughtful approach to working with artists, stakeholders and collections, alongside a commitment to best practice in collections care and access. Key skills include excellent organisation and documentation, the ability to coordinate complex projects and installations across multiple sites, and strong written and verbal communication skills to engage a wide range of audiences. You will be confident managing competing priorities, solving problems independently, and working effectively within a small, collaborative team. We are particularly interested in candidates who are passionate about widening access to art, developing inclusive interpretation and exploring how collections can support teaching, research and community engagement. An interest in digital engagement and new forms of interpretation will also be valuable. While relevant experience is welcome, we encourage application from individuals who can demonstrate transferable skills, recognising that not all candidates will have had equal access to opportunities within the sector. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department Warwick Arts Centre is the largest purpose-built arts centre outside London. Opened in 1974 and situated at the heart of the University of Warwick, in Coventry, we're home to a variety of spaces including a concert hall, theatre, two studios, three cinemas and an art gallery. Almost one million people visit us every year, with many more engaging in our activities across communities and other spaces. We're passionate about the arts, and how it has the power to move, connect, inspire and present new possibilities; we're here to amplify under-represented voices, nurture the next generation of creatives, and serve as a vibrant and welcoming social hub for all. Warwick Arts Centre is committed to building a diverse and inclusive workforce. We particularly welcome applications from people who are currently underrepresented in the arts sector, including people of Global Majority heritage, those from lower socio-economic backgrounds, and disabled people. We recognise that a greater diversity of backgrounds, experiences and perspectives enriches the arts and strengthens our organisation. Purpose – We’re here to share our love for the arts. Belief – We believe the arts are a place we can all meet - a place to share our experiences, a place to find common ground and understanding, a place to connect and have the courage to transform and explore new possibilities together. Promise – Experiences you’ll feel and never forget -- be it joy, excitement or sadness and whoever you are, wherever you’re from. You can find out more about our vision and values at https://www.warwickartscentre.co.uk/our-vision/ About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 106 th in the world and 8th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2024 , Guardian University Guide 2025 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 20th September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To submit an application, please visit the Warwick Employment Group by copying and pasting the below into your browser: https://www.warwickemploymentgroup.com/job/Curator%20(Art%20Collection)/851e8a91-560f-4114-8c64-23a7d73a3661 We recommend following the below guidance to best support your application: Review the Job Description, Person Specification, Job Pack and information listed on the University of Warwick’s advert page. Consider all the different types of roles you have had or work that you have done to support your application. For the essential criterion, it would be helpful to provide evidence/an example of what you have done that demonstrates that you have the experience, skills or knowledge we are looking for. Remember to tell us why you want to work for Warwick Arts Centre. Look at our website to make sure that you understand the range, scope and scale of our work. Explore our context and our role in the region. Consider the potential users of Warwick Arts Centre and how best to communicate its activity. Ask a friend/colleague to review your application and to check that you have provided examples and told the best story of your career to date and your ambitions in this role and the future. What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 26 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion Equality, Diversity, & Inclusion Warwick is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive and respectful community where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all backgrounds, cultures, and communities, and actively encourage candidates from underrepresented groups to apply. Find out more about our Social Inclusion work at Warwick . Find out more about our awards and accreditations . We are also one of the six founder institutions of the EUTOPIA European University Alliance . Safeguarding & DBS The University of Warwick is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of all those we work with. Roles involving regulated activity are subject to a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check at the appropriate level, in line with the DBS Code of Practice. The University will ensure that anyone subject to a barring order does not undertake any work with the barred group (children and/or adults). All employees, volunteers, and partners are expected to share our commitment to safeguarding. Rehabilitation of Ex-Offenders The University will not discriminate against applicants who make a disclosure relating to a conviction. Disclosures at application stage are only visible to the DBS team, not to hiring panels. This ensures fairness and removes bias from the shortlisting process. Job Description JD - Curator (Art Collection) (20621).pdf – 190KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. Cookies"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4548-Taught-Programmes-Coordinator-x2-21888-0726/en-GB": {
      "title": "Taught Programmes Coordinator x2 (21888-0726)",
      "description": "Taught Programmes Coordinator x2 (21888-0726) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Taught Programmes Coordinator x2 (21888-0726) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Mathematics Position Type Permanent Salary £26,707 to £30,378 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Frances Pinches, Taught Programmes Officer, at F.E.Pinches@warwick.ac.uk Warwick Mathematics Institute has two vacancies for full-time, campus-based, Taught Programmes Coordinators to join our student facing team which supports our undergraduate and taught masters students’ education and their wider student experience. The WMI is a large, vibrant department, and this role, based in a modern, purpose built space on the central University Campus, presents a good opportunity for someone wishing to extend their administrative skills within an academic environment with a culture of excellence and continuous improvement. About You The successful applicant will be an adaptable team player with a professional approach, initiative, excellent interpersonal skills, attention to detail, high standards of accuracy and proficiency in relevant IT. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department Warwick Mathematics Institute is a world-class department within a globally renowned university. We are recognised for our academic excellence and our connectivity to the wider university. We offer a broad range of undergraduate and postgraduate courses. We recruit the brightest students, offer exceptional learning experiences, have a positive impact on society, produce impactful research that is published in premier journals and employ outstanding faculty who are global experts in their fields. Our historical strengths in pure mathematics are now complemented by increasingly broad coverage of applied subjects. We run a wide range of weekly seminar series, and many workshops and conferences. We have a friendly Professional Services Team of approximately 30 staff who provide the administrative support to ensure the department can successfully deliver on all it offers in a professional and positive way. The Professional Services Team includes, but is not limited to, a Taught Programmes team who support our undergraduate and postgraduate taught students; teams working to support our postgraduate research students; an Outreach team who are responsible for supporting schools and colleges in the teaching and learning of mathematics in the local region, with the aim to increase participation in Core Maths, AS and A Level Maths and Further Maths; the Finance team and a team who work in the Mathematics Research Centre (MRC), which is there to support our large programme of academic seminars, workshops and conferences. More information on colleagues in the department can be found at https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/maths/people/staff/ . The department encourages the personal and professional development of all its staff and we are committed to fostering an inclusive environment. In particular, we are working hard towards improving our gender balance; we currently hold a Bronze Athena Swan award and our energetic Equality, Diversity, and Inclusion committee plays a significant role in shaping departmental policy. For further information about the Maths department please visit our website: https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/maths/ . About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 6th September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. In your cover letter, please address each essential criterion and any relevant desirable criteria listed in the job description, providing clear and specific examples that demonstrate how you meet each requirement through your skills, experience, knowledge, and achievements.** Interview Date: To be confirmed Start Date: To be confirmed * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 26 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD - Taught Programmes Coordinator x2 (21888, 104504).pdf – 120KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4521-Programmes-Assistant-UG-and-PG-Programmes-102047-0726/en-GB": {
      "title": "Programmes Assistant (UG and PG Programmes) (102047-0726)",
      "description": "Programmes Assistant (UG and PG Programmes) (102047-0726) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Programmes Assistant (UG and PG Programmes) (102047-0726) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Physics Position Type Permanent Salary £26,707 to £30,378 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Helen Murray (Educational Support Services Manager) at helen.murray@warwick.ac.uk. Flexible Working We welcome applications from candidates seeking part-time employment (ideally minimum 0.8FTE) or other flexible working basis (e.g. job share), despite the position being advertised as full-time. This supports our commitment to providing and supporting an inclusive culture where individuals are valued, respected and treated equally. The Department of Physics seeks to appoint a permanent full-time Programmes Assistant to support their busy Student Office. This role will provide general clerical support for the delivery of teaching and learning to all undergraduate (UG) and postgraduate (PG) students in the Department. This is an excellent opportunity to join a well-established team and gain experience in both UG and PG student administration. You will be involved in a diverse range of activities associated with supporting admissions, teaching and research activities and working in a large academic department. Full training will be provided as appropriate. Whilst training you will be expected to be working all of your working hours in the office. There may be scope for some hybrid working later, but as this is a student-facing role, the majority of the time will be spent on campus. About You We are looking for someone with outstanding customer service skills and the willingness and enthusiasm to provide the very best standards of student support. You will also have excellent communication skills as regular liaison with internal and external people will be necessary. You do not need to have previous experience of working within the university or working in a student-facing role to apply. An ability to organise conferences and other events including travel arrangements is essential. You must be able to prioritise your own workload, and to use your own initiative to work independently as well as within a team. You will have excellent organisational, administrative and IT skills with good working experience of Microsoft Office packages and an ability to quickly learn and use new IT systems. Knowledge of Sitebuilder web software is desirable. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department Department of Physics The post will be based in the Student Office team in the Department of Physics, a vibrant academic department with over 200 academic, research, technical and professional services staff, over 800 undergraduate students and 200 postgraduate research students. We are proud of our diverse community of staff, students, and visitors, and are committed to maintaining excellence in both teaching and research by promoting equality of  opportunity for all, within a culture of mutual respect and dignity. We are pleased to hold an Athena SWAN Silver Award, recognising our ongoing work to advance gender equality  for all staff and students. We also hold an Institute of Physics Inclusion Award in support of our commitment to creating a welcoming and inclusive environment. Further information about working in the Department of Physics and the benefits available can be found at www.warwick.ac.uk/physics/staff/working/ . Childcare for interviews Childcare can be provided for you at the University of Warwick Nursery ( www.warwick.ac.uk/services/childrensservices/nursery ) in order for you to attend the interview. Childcare is subject to availability of places at the Nursery. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 6th September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: To be confirmed Start Date: As soon as possible * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 26 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD Programmes Assistant (UG and PG Programmes) (102047).pdf – 131KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4691-Marie-Curie-Early-Stage-Researcher-Poseidon-112049-0826/en-GB": {
      "title": "Marie Curie Early Stage Researcher (Poseidon) (112049-0826)",
      "description": "Marie Curie Early Stage Researcher (Poseidon) (112049-0826) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Marie Curie Early Stage Researcher (Poseidon) (112049-0826) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department School of Engineering Position Type Fixed Term Duration Fixed term contract until 31st July 2029 Salary £39,600 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Xueyu Geng (Professor) at Xueyu.geng@warwick.ac.uk. One full time (36.5 hrs/week) Fixed Term position to end on 31 July 2029.  Start date will align to PhD enrolment dates. Please note: the salary advertised covers a range of allowances and pension enrolments. Final salary will be dependent on entitlement to these allowances. The School of Engineering is looking to appoint a Early Stage Marie Curie Researcher to undertake high-quality research within the MSCA Doctoral Network POSEIDON ( https://poseidon-dn.eu/ ). The postholder will be assisting in developing the next generation of ecofriendly offshore windfarms and closely collaborating with academic and industrial partners across the EU to deliver the scientific and training objectives of the project. The successful candidate will undertake innovative research focused on addressing key challenges in sustainable offshore wind development, contributing to improved understanding, design and performance of offshore wind infrastructure and its interaction with the marine environment. They will also have opportunities to develop their research skills through collaboration across the POSEIDON network, international secondments and dedicated training activities. This post will have heavy emphasis on data science & ML programming applied to large environmental datasets (geospatial, weather, tide). This is an excellent opportunity for an early-career researcher to gain international research experience, develop a strong academic and industrial network, and contribute to the transition towards more sustainable offshore renewable energy. About You A MSc or equivalent in Civil/Geotechnical Engineering, Ocean/Offshore Engineering, Applied Mechanics, Naval Architecture, or a closely related discipline You should evidence the ability to deliver independent research, and strong potential for high-quality research, with a developing profile and an understanding of relevant methods and techniques. Strong numerical and computational skills, plus proficiency in at least one of: Python, MATLAB, or C++, particularly for data analysis, automation, or machine learning implementation is essential, as is previous experience with computational mechanics and laboratory and physical tests for soil characterisation. You will be a collaborative and motivated individual, able to work effectively with partners across Europe and willing to undertake international secondments. Strong communication skills (in English), excellent IT proficiency, and the ability to deliver work on time are essential. Candidates will be required to meet Marie Curie Early Stage Researcher eligibility criteria which includes: At, applicants must not have been awarded a PhD. Candidates should not have lived or carried out their main activity in the UK for more than 12 months in the 3 years immediately before their recruitment. Applicants must be in the first four years (full-time equivalent research experience) of their research career You will be registered for a PhD degree at the University of Warwick. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department This post is based in the School of Engineering at the University of Warwick, within Professor Xueyu Geng’s Built Environment and Sustainability Research Cluster. The School of Engineering is committed to the principles of the Athena SWAN Charter, which recognises work undertaken to address gender equality, representation and progression for all staff working in an academic environment. The School currently holds the Athena SWAN Gold award and the University holds an Institutional Silver award. Further information about the work of the School in relation to Equality and Athena SWAN can be found at https://warwick.ac.uk/fac/sci/eng/about/equality_and_diversity/ About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 6 September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include a CV and Cover Letter. These documents should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: To be confirmed Start Date: As soon as possible * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 30 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD Marie Curie Early Stage Researcher (112049).pdf – 112KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK and/or are seeking sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa, please follow this link which contains further information about obtaining the right to work in the UK. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
