    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4562-Senior-Business-Analyst-Online-Programme-Management-111916-0726/en-GB": {
      "title": "Senior Business Analyst",
      "description": "Senior Business Analyst - Online Programme Management (111916-0726) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Senior Business Analyst - Online Programme Management (111916-0726) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Information & Digital Group Position Type Fixed Term Duration Fixed-term contract for 16 months Salary Competitive About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Pete Hampshire, Recruitment Manager, at Pete.Hampshire@warwick.ac.uk . As a Senior Business Analyst within the Information and Digital Group (IDG), you will play a key role in delivering the University of Warwick’s Online Programme Management (OPM) initiative, a major transformation supporting the University’s online learning strategy and the development of high-quality digital education. Working at the forefront of early-stage programme delivery, you will translate strategic intent into clear, actionable requirements, helping to shape solutions and lay the foundations for sustainable change. You will lead Discovery activities to define business needs, map current and future states, and provide evidence-based recommendations to inform decision-making across a complex and evolving landscape. Operating as part of a programme team, across multiple workstreams, you will collaborate with senior stakeholders, academic departments, and professional services to bring clarity, structure, and momentum to a high-profile transformation programme. This role offers a unique opportunity to influence how online and digital education is designed and delivered at Warwick, particularly suited to individuals who thrive in ambiguity and can operate effectively at both strategic and operational levels. About You You will bring significant experience of business analysis in complex environments, with the confidence to influence at senior levels and across diverse stakeholder groups. You are skilled at applying structured analysis to deliver clarity and actionable insight across an evolving landscape. Your communication and relationship‑building skills enable you to work effectively across academic and professional services communities. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department To find out more about the Information & Digital Group at the University of Warwick, please visit our website . About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply To submit an application, please visit Warwick Employment Group using the link below: https://www.warwickemploymentgroup.com/job/Senior%20Business%20Analyst%20(OPM)/2c565469-c07a-4430-96b5-1413f341c0ee What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 30 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD - Senior Business Analyst - Online Programme Man (111916).pdf – 108KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK and/or are seeking sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa, please follow this link which contains further information about obtaining the right to work in the UK. Cookies"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4242-Delivery-Manager-110113-0526/en-GB": {
      "title": "Delivery Manager (110113-0526)",
      "description": "Delivery Manager (110113-0526) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Delivery Manager (110113-0526) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Information & Digital Group - Portfolio Delivery Position Type Fixed Term Duration Fixed-term contract for 18 months Salary £47,389 to £56,535 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Pete Hampshire, Recruitment Manager, at Pete.Hampshire@warwick.ac.uk . Are you tempted by joining a top 10 UK University as it celebrates 60 years of commitment to innovation and impact, backed by pioneering research, challenging teaching and a drive to find new solutions to the complex challenges facing our region and the world? Are you motivated by the opportunity to shape digital experiences at a leading UK university? At Warwick, we are proud of our reputation for innovation, impact, and delivering real-world change — and our digital services are central to that ambition. The Information & Digital Group (IDG) is driving a major transformation of how the University designs, builds and delivers its web and digital platforms. As part of this, we are investing in the evolution of our web estate — improving usability, accessibility, performance and scalability across services used by thousands of students, staff and external audiences every day. We are looking for a Delivery Manager to play a critical role in this work. Why Join Us? Be part of a forward-thinking team driving digital innovation in higher education. Work on cutting-edge technologies that directly impact thousands of staff and students. Collaborate in a supportive, inclusive environment that values creativity and continuous improvement. Enjoy excellent benefits, flexible working, and the opportunity to grow your career at a world-class institution. This is an opportunity to: Shape the future of Warwick’s web and digital services. Work in a complex, intellectually stimulating environment. Deliver change that has a visible impact across the University community. About You You are an experienced Delivery Manager who thrives in complex, fast-paced environments where priorities evolve and clarity must be actively shaped. You bring a proven ability to lead delivery across multidisciplinary teams, working confidently with technical specialists, product leads, and senior stakeholders to ensure progress is structured, transparent, and focused on outcomes. You are comfortable navigating ambiguity, making informed decisions, and maintaining momentum across multiple workstreams. You build strong relationships quickly, communicate clearly, and are able to challenge constructively to drive the best outcomes. Above all, you take ownership — bringing energy, accountability, and a pragmatic approach to delivery that balances rigour with flexibility. This is not a passive delivery role. You will be expected to: Drive progress and momentum across complex delivery environments. Establish clarity where ambiguity exists and shape delivery approaches accordingly. Manage dependencies, risks and competing priorities across teams and suppliers. Ensure that delivery is aligned to strategic objectives and delivers measurable value. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department The Information & Digital Group is responsible for a new University Digital Strategy to support the University’s ambitions to be world-class in all it does.  IDG is central to the delivery of the University strategy by providing a high quality service to all of our stakeholders, enabling the University to prioritise its requirements, and to deliver this service in a manner that maximises value at every stage. IDG strives to provide excellent, highly responsive relationships and partnerships, to be innovative leaders with vision and strategy, to provide enterprise architecture that drives innovation across the institution, to delivery products and projects on time, cost and quality through services that always meet service level agreements.  We need to operate in an increasingly agile, digital-first environment, being able to quickly assess risk and seize opportunity. The IDG Portfolio Delivery team defines the processes, tools and standards for all IDG programmes thereby ensuring delivery to time, cost & quality. The team ensure the delivery of projects, products and platforms that provide tangible value, outcomes and benefits to the university. Portfolio Delivery also creates great experiences by delivering at the right speed and in close collaboration with the University. About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply To submit an application, please visit Warwick Employment Group using the link below: https://www.warwickemploymentgroup.com/job/Delivery%20Manager%20(Web%20Evolution%20Programme)/5e3132e8-d5eb-4435-9c84-416aa5a50f87 What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 30 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD Delivery Manager (110113).pdf – 144KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK and/or are seeking sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa, please follow this link which contains further information about obtaining the right to work in the UK. Cookies"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4672-Director-of-Marketing-and-Communications-108350-0826/en-GB": {
      "title": "Director of Marketing and Communications (108350-0826)",
      "description": "Director of Marketing and Communications (108350-0826) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Director of Marketing and Communications (108350-0826) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department WMG Position Type Permanent Salary Competitive About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries, please contact Ellis Toyne (People Partner) at Ellis.Toyne@warwick.ac.uk Flexible Working We will consider applications for employment on a part-time or other flexible working basis (e.g. job share), despite the position being advertised as full-time. This is an exciting opportunity to lead the marketing and communications for one of the University of Warwick’s largest and most innovative academic departments.  The successful candidate will lead a team of around 20 marketing and communications professionals, who deliver campaigns, content and collateral to support student recruitment, engage industry partners and attract research funding.  The role is broad and varied, protecting and building a brand that has led collaboration between industry and academia for 45 years.  It carries responsibility for all aspects of strategic communications, digital channels, events and paid activity, as well as membership of WMG’s senior leadership team. About You We’re looking for an experienced marketing and communications leader.   The successful candidate will have a breadth of experience and skills covering communications, digital, brand, events and paid media – they will know how to integrate different channels and activities to maximise impact to a variety of audiences.  They will have excellent leadership skills: able to bring out the best in a highly-skilled team, providing direction and clarity of priorities; they’ll also be able to work effectively with a wide range of stakeholders, from academics to fellow professional service personnel. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department The Warwick Manufacturing Group (WMG) is the largest department at the University of Warwick, with over 800 staff and nearly 3,000 students across undergraduate and postgraduate programmes in management, technology, and applied engineering. We are globally recognised for our world-class research, innovative industry partnerships, and teaching excellence, and we are proud holders of the Athena SWAN Silver Award and the Institutional Silver Award. Find out more about the High Value Manufacturing Catapult centre . Find out more about the Energy Innovation Centre . Find out more about our range of undergraduate and apprenticeship degrees here . About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 6th September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: 23rd September 2026 Start Date: To be confirmed * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 30 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion Equality, Diversity, & Inclusion Warwick is committed to fostering a diverse, inclusive and respectful community where everyone can thrive. We welcome applications from all backgrounds, cultures, and communities, and actively encourage candidates from underrepresented groups to apply. Find out more about our Social Inclusion work at Warwick . Find out more about our awards and accreditations . We are also one of the six founder institutions of the EUTOPIA European University Alliance . Safeguarding & DBS The University of Warwick is committed to safeguarding and promoting the welfare of all those we work with. Roles involving regulated activity are subject to a Disclosure and Barring Service (DBS) check at the appropriate level, in line with the DBS Code of Practice. The University will ensure that anyone subject to a barring order does not undertake any work with the barred group (children and/or adults). All employees, volunteers, and partners are expected to share our commitment to safeguarding. Rehabilitation of Ex-Offenders The University will not discriminate against applicants who make a disclosure relating to a conviction. Disclosures at application stage are only visible to the DBS team, not to hiring panels. This ensures fairness and removes bias from the shortlisting process. Job Description JD Director of Marketing, Communications and Advocacy (108350).pdf – 129KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK and/or are seeking sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa, please follow this link which contains further information about obtaining the right to work in the UK. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
    },
    "https://warwick-careers.tal.net/vx/lang-en-GB/mobile-0/appcentre-1/brand-4/user-11595/xf-0a29ed012b2b/candidate/so/pm/1/pl/3/opp/4538-Apprentice-Gardener-106182-0726/en-GB": {
      "title": "Apprentice Gardener (106182-0726)",
      "description": "Apprentice Gardener (106182-0726) - University of Warwick By clicking \"I accept\" you consent to the use of cookies on our website to support technical features and anonymous statistics I accept I accept the cookie policy Opt Out I would like to opt out of cookies Read more Read more about our cookie policy Skip to content (Opens in a new window) Login Create Account HOME OPPORTUNITIES HELP CENTRE Login Create Account Apprentice Gardener (106182-0726) Location University of Warwick Campus, Coventry Department Estates Position Type Apprenticeship Salary £15,593 - £23,915 per annum About the Role Informal Queries For informal queries about the role, please contact Kelly Baker (Head of Landscape and Operations) at Kelly.Baker@warwick.ac.uk. If you have a keen interest in learning about all aspects of gardening including the use of machinery, then look no further! Warwick University and is looking to take on an apprentice within their Gardens Team. About You You will be able to work within the organisation’s working hours/pattern between the hours of 8am to 4pm on a 5-day basis. Required to attend college as required and complete coursework in a timely manner as part of the apprenticeship scheme.  Prepared to work towards an Intermediate Apprenticeship in Horticulture (NVQ Level 2). You will be Educated to GCSE level or equivalent, including English and Maths grade 4-9. When applying please indicate how you meet the essential criteria on the Person Specification. For details on the experience and skills required, please refer to the job description attached as a PDF below. About the Department The University of Warwick consists of three adjacent sites including Central campus, Gibbet Hill campus and Westwood campus. The Gardens team manage over 715 acres of plant collections including herbaceous borders, tree collections, newly landscaped areas, woodlands, and lakes. During the apprenticeship, you will be working in an award-winning landscape on a range of exciting soft landscaping projects. You will work alongside the team, helping them to maintain and develop the grounds and gardens of the University campus. We provide a comprehensive training scheme where you will have mentors to support you along the way and if you put in the hard work, we will help you achieve your apprenticeship with flying colours. We offer a two-year apprenticeship starting in September 2026. The training will be a mixture of online sessions with regular visits to college. Any required travel to college will be covered by the University of Warwick. https://warwick.ac.uk/services/estates/departments/facilities/grounds_and_gardens/ About the University We are a world-leading research-intensive university founded in 1965. We are ranked 74th in the world and 9th in the UK. * Additionally, 92% of our research is rated world-leading or internationally excellent .** Find out more about us at warwick.ac.uk/about/ . * World University Ranking 2026 , Complete University Guide 2026 ** Research Excellence Framework 2021 How to Apply Closing Deadline: Sunday 6th September 2026 at 11:55pm (UK Time)* To apply, please click APPLY below and submit an application form by the closing deadline. You will be asked to include two attachments: CV Cover Letter These should: Outline employment and education history (including your most recent employment). Demonstrate how you meet the essential and desirable criteria in the Job Description using clear examples. Please ensure your application clearly evidences the essential criteria, as the hiring panel may not be able to shortlist your application if these are not demonstrated.** Interview Date: To be confirmed Start Date: September 2026 * Applications must be submitted through the warwick-careers.tal.net portal before the closing deadline. We recommend completing your application form in good time, as the advert will automatically close at the deadline. ** You are welcome to include any career breaks, such as parental leave, caring responsibilities, or long-term sickness absence. For guidance on how to format a cover letter, see here . What we Offer We provide a comprehensive range of benefits, including: An attractive pension scheme. 26 days holiday plus University Christmas closure. Generous parental/adoption leave policy. Onsite childcare facilities. Excellent learning and development opportunities. We recognise the importance of a healthy work/life balance and offer access to flexible working arrangements. Where possible, we offer hybrid working arrangements that combine office-based and remote working. Opportunities for hybrid working will depend on the requirements of the role, business needs of the department and can be discussed during the recruitment process. For more information, see here . We are proud to be a Living Wage employer . Our Commitment to Inclusion To find out more about our commitments to equality, diversity, and inclusion, please see: Our Commitments | University of Warwick Job Description JD - Apprentice Gardener (106182).pdf – 108KB Opens in a new window Right to Work in the UK We wish to advise applicants that this role is not eligible for sponsorship for a Skilled Worker visa. If you do not yet have the right to work in the UK you will need to check the UK Government Website to see if you are eligible to obtain the right to work in the UK through one of the other UK immigration routes before you make your application. Cookies Accessibility & Cookie Policy"
